  "source_dataset": "MIMIC_IV_NOTE",
  "text": "Allergies:\nPenicillins / hydrocodone / ampicillin / codeine / hydromorphone\n\nChief Complaint:\nNSTEMI and emergent CABG consultation\n\nHistory of Present Illness:\n___ with Type I DM c/b ESRD on HD, Atrial fibrillation not on \ncoumadin, HTN, HLD who presented to ___ with hypotension \nand troponinemia and underwent cath showing multivessel CAD and \nelevated RH pressures, now transferred to ___ for CABG eval. \n\nShe reports that since the past year she has had worsening SOB \nand dyspnea. At baseline she is unable to drive herself, is SOB \nwith walking to her bathroom and is markedly SOB with climbing \none set of stairs. She reports that she has had worsening SOB \nand ___ edema. She has had difficulty with dialysis recently and \nhad three days of dialysis in a row. Following her last dialysis \nsession on ___ she felt weak, dizzy and SOB. She was \northostatic with SBP in the 90. EMS was called and an EKG showed \nnew afib w/ ST depression in I and AVF. An initial troponin I \nwas .44 which climbed to above 1.  She was admitted for an \nNSTEMI and started on a heparin gtt. She was taken to the cath \nlab the following day. Coronary catheterization showed 80%dLM, \npRCA100%, 80%mLAD, subtotal occluded Cx and an EF 20%. A RHC \nshowed elevated filling pressures so an IABP was placed and she \nwas transferred to ___ for Csurg eval. On arrival, she is \ncomfortable and in no acute distress. She is mentating well.\n\nBrief Hospital Course:\n___ with Type I DM c/b ESRD on HD, Atrial fibrillation not on \ncoumadin, HTN, HLD who presented to ___ with hypotension \nand troponinemia and underwent cath showing multivessel CAD and \nelevated RH pressures, now transferred to ___ for CABG \nevaluation and pending CABG on ___.\n\n# CORONARIES: 80%dLM, pRCA100%, 80%mLAD, subtotal occluded Cx, \n# PUMP: EF 20%\n# RHYTHM:  atrial fibrillation, NSR\n\n#) CORONARY ARTERY DISEASE: Patient presented with elevated \ntroponin and SOB in the setting of hypotension following \naggressive dialysis. She was found to have three vessel coronary \nartery disease.  IABP removed ___. Patient was stabilized in \nthe CCU and transferred to cardiac surgery for CABG on ___.\nShe was continued on ASA 81mg daily, Atorvastatin 80mg daily, \nBB, heparin gtt. In addition, Csurg recs were followed including \nlab monitoring, mupirocin, MSSA swab, carotid ultrasound, and \ncrossmatch + type/screen.\n \n\n#) VOLUME OVERLOAD: Patient has chronic SOB and is able to pass \nin the setting of renal failure and heart failure, outlined \nbelow. \n\n#) ACUTE DECOMPENSATED SYSTOLIC HEART FAILURE: EF of 20%. Likely \nsecondary to ischemia. She reports that she able to climb one \nflight of stairs before having to catch her breath. See TTE in \nresults section. Ensure daily weights, strict I/Os.\n \n#) ESRD ON HD: Patient is currently on HD ___. She is \ncurrently a candidate for kidney transplant. continue sevalamer. \ncontinue cinacalcet. \n\n#) IDDM TYPE I: c/b nephropathy, neuropathy, retinopathy. \nPatient is not on any long acting insulin. Unknown HgbA1c. \nInsulin sliding scale as inpatient, see HgbA1c in results \nsection. Diabetic diet. \n\n# MACROCYTIC ANEMIA: Likely secondary to ESRD. Trend HCT, f/u \niron, B12, folate.\n\n# GERD: continue omeprazole\n\n# HYPOTHYROIDISM: continue levothyroxine supplementation.\n\n# FEN: avoid IVF, replete lytes, NPO until procedural plan \ndecided.\n# ACCESS: PIV's, IABP\n# PROPHYLAXIS:  \n- DVT PPX with heparin gtt \n- Pain management with tylenol\n- Bowel regimen with senna colace\n\n# CODE: Full  \n# ___ consult: after IABP pulled\n# ICU consent: done \n# CONTACT:  Son - ___ ___\n# DISPO: CCU, pending Above \n\nPost-operative course:\n\nPatiet was taken to the OR ___ with pre-op EF 20% and she \nunderwent CABGx3 LIMA-LAD, SVG-PDA, SVG-OM. Intraop course \ncomplicated by hemodynamic instability coming off pump, required \nopen cardiac massage,  crash back on pump and IABP placed.Please \nsee intraoperative note for further details. She arrived from \nthe OR with chest closed, significant hemodynamic instability \nwith IABP 1:1 on Epi, levo, vaso and neo gtts. Her \npost-operative course remained complicated due to profound on \ngoing cardiogenic shock. Chroic renal failure and due to \ninstability she was started on CVVH therapy. She required \ninhaled nitric oxide.  Her chest was reopened at bedside on \nPOD#4. Interventional cardiology Dr ___ was consulted, \nregarding percutaneous RVAD placement. She was not an ECMO \ncandidate. RVAD was placed. Even despite placement her \nhemodynamics did not improve and infact she deteriorated soon \nafterwards. Her pacing wires lost capture,dopamine was added, \nher chest was reexplored. She regained capture but continued to \nbe hemodynamically unstable and in profound cardiogenic shock \nwith acute end organ damage, coagulopathic and thrombcytopenic.  \nDiscussion with family including son ___ who is the health \ncare proxy was held, and the decesion was made to terminate \ncare. Patiet died on ___ @ 16:26 with family at bedside. No \nME examination.\n\nDischarge Diagnosis:\nexpired",
